# Local, untracked Make overrides. Copy to `Makefile.local` (gitignored) and set your
# private-registry host — keeping the internal hostname out of this public tree:
#
#   cp Makefile.local.example Makefile.local     # then edit the host below
#
# The private registry hosts the immutable :sha-<commit> and :VERSION images (pushed by
# dev-deploy / release, pulled by the dev and prod stacks), plus the luxarch (make arch) and
# luxlint (make lint / format) guard images. Without Makefile.local the local + e2e
# stacks still build from source, and make arch / make lint skip gracefully.
#
# `:=`, not `?=`: an exported REGISTRY in the shell (sourcing an .env file that sets
# REGISTRY=ghcr.io, say) would otherwise win, and publish-sha/release would push an unscanned
# candidate to that registry. A command-line `make … REGISTRY=…` still overrides `:=`.
REGISTRY           := docker.your-registry.example:5000
LUXARCH_REGISTRY   := docker.your-registry.example:5000
LUXLINT_REGISTRY   := docker.your-registry.example:5000
LUXAUDIT_REGISTRY  := docker.your-registry.example:5000
